 "instruction": "Remove two fabrications and one heavy import.\n\n**1. `EmotionAnalyzer` is a stub** (`sanctuary/mind/voice_analyzer.py`). `analyze_segment` returns \"neutral\" at confidence 0.95 whatever the audio, even silence. Replace it with a real prosodic analysis in numpy (no model, no network):\n- Constructor: `EmotionAnalyzer(sample_rate=16000)`. Keep `emotion_states`, the `current_context` defaults (neutral, confidence 0.0), `update_context` and `get_current_context` as they are.\n- `analyze_segment(audio_data, sample_rate=None)`:\n  - Empty audio raises `ValueError`.\n  - Return `primary_emotion` (one of `emotion_states`), `confidence` (a Python float in [0, 1]), `secondary_emotions`, `arousal` and `valence` (both in [0, 1]), and `features`.\n  - `features` includes at least `zcr`, `voiced_ratio`, `f0_mean`, `pitch_norm`, `f0_cv` and `energy_cv`.\n- **Suggested approach:** short-time frames (about 40 ms, 20 ms hop), a per-frame pitch estimate from normalized autocorrelation restricted to the voice band (about 80–400 Hz), a frame counted as voiced when its autocorrelation peak is high enough, plus energy and pitch variation across frames. Map the features to arousal and valence, then to an emotion.\n- **Required behavior:**\n  - Silence reads neutral with confidence under 0.1. Confidence must be earned by real voiced structure, so a clean periodic tone is more confident than white noise.\n  - A 320 Hz tone reads more aroused than a 120 Hz tone.\n  - A pitch-sweeping, amplitude-modulated signal reads more aroused than a steady low tone.\n\n**2. `LazyEmbeddingCache` fabricates embeddings** (`sanctuary/performance/lazy_embeddings.py`). With no `compute_fn` it silently falls back to a hash-based pseudo-embedding, which would corrupt every similarity built on the cache.\n- Constructing it without `compute_fn` now raises `ValueError`. The message says to pass a real embedder, or `LazyEmbeddingCache.deterministic_test_embedding` in tests.\n- Rename the hash function to the static method `deterministic_test_embedding(text) -> list[float]`, with a docstring saying it is for tests only. It must stay deterministic.\n- Update existing callers and tests that relied on the default.\n\n**3.** `sanctuary/mind/speech_processor.py` imports `transformers` at module level. Import it lazily, where `WhisperProcessor` loads its model, so the module (and `EmotionAnalyzer`, which it uses) can be imported without transformers installed.",
